    <bpmn:process id="W_W1342" name="W1342. Real-Time Gross Settlement (RTGS) &amp; High-Value Payment Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vendor payment &gt; PHP 5M per W7; payroll disbursement per W10; intercompany fund transfer &gt; PHP 10M; tax payment &gt; PHP 5M; or emergency payment requiring same-day settlement
Frequency: ~15–25 RTGS transactions per month; ~5–10 high-value intercompany transfers per month
Volume: ~20–35 RTGS transactions/month totaling ~PHP 800M–1.5B; average transaction PHP 30M–50M
Owner: Treasury Manager
Participants: Treasury Analyst, CFO, CEO (for payments &gt; PHP 20M), AP Supervisor, Bank Relationship Manager
Source: workflow W1342 — Real-Time Gross Settlement (RTGS) &amp; High-Value Payment Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1342_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1342_Lane1" name="AP Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1342_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1342_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1342_Lane2" name="Treasury Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1342_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1342_Lane3" name="CFO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1342_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1342_Lane4" name="Treasury Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1342_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1342_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1342_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1342_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1342_Start6" name="Vendor payment &gt; PHP 5M per W7; payroll disbursement per W10; intercompany fund transfer…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1342_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1342_Task7" name="Payment initiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Payment initiation: AP Supervisor or Treasury Analyst initiates high-value payment in ERP: (a) select payment type: vendor payment, intercompany transfer, payroll, tax payment, (b) enter payment details: beneficiary name, bank account number, bank name (BSP-member bank), amount, payment reference, purpose, (c) attach supporting documentation: approved invoice (vendor), Board Resolution (intercompany), BIR tax return (tax), payroll register (payroll), (d) system validates: vendor master match, bank account format (Philippine bank account validation), payment purpose per entity policy, (e) system flags payment as &quot;RTGS required&quot; if amount &gt; PHP 5M or payment type requires same-day settlement
Responsible (R): AP Supervisor / Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1342_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1342_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1342_Task8" name="First-level verification (Maker)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: First-level verification (Maker): Treasury Manager reviews payment in ERP: (a) verify beneficiary details match supporting documentation, (b) verify amount matches approved invoice/transfer request, (c) verify bank account matches vendor master per W320 payment anomaly detection, (d) confirm RTGS is appropriate (vs. standard PESONet batch transfer for non-urgent payments), (e) approve payment — system locks details from further modification
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1342_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1342_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1342_Task9" name="Second-level authorization (Authorizer)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Second-level authorization (Authorizer): CFO authorizes high-value payment: (a) for payments PHP 5M–20M: CFO reviews and authorizes via bank portal or ERP-to-bank integration, (b) for payments &gt; PHP 20M: CEO and CFO dual authorization per W320.3 — both must authorize independently in bank portal, (c) authorizer reviews: payment summary, beneficiary, amount, supporting documentation reference, (d) system records authorizer ID, timestamp, and authorization level for audit trail
Responsible (R): CFO / CEO
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1342_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1342_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1342_Task10" name="RTGS submission">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: RTGS submission: Treasury Analyst submits payment to bank via electronic banking portal: (a) log into bank portal (dual-login for security per W320), (b) enter or confirm payment details in bank RTGS module, (c) bank validates: beneficiary bank is BSP-member, sufficient account balance, cut-off time compliance (BSP PhilPaSS cut-off: 3:30 PM for same-day settlement), (d) bank submits to PhilPaSS for real-time settlement, (e) bank confirms settlement with PhilPaSS reference number
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1342_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1342_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1342_Task11" name="Settlement confirmation &amp; reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Settlement confirmation &amp; reconciliation: (a) Treasury Analyst obtains settlement confirmation from bank portal: PhilPaSS reference number, settlement timestamp, amount, beneficiary, (b) record settlement in treasury management system: PhilPaSS reference, payment reference, settlement status = &quot;Settled&quot;, (c) update cash position per W30 — high-value payment immediately reflected in daily cash position, (d) for vendor payments: update AP invoice status to &quot;Paid&quot; per W7, (e) for intercompany transfers: update intercompany account per W17, (f) file settlement confirmation for audit trail per W120
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1342_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1342_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1342_Task12" name="Failed/rejected payment handling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Failed/rejected payment handling: If RTGS payment is rejected: (a) bank returns payment with rejection reason: insufficient funds, invalid beneficiary account, bank system error, past cut-off time, (b) Treasury Analyst investigates and resolves: (i) insufficient funds: arrange intraday liquidity via credit facility or fund transfer from another account, (ii) invalid account: contact beneficiary to verify bank details, (iii) past cut-off: resubmit next business day or arrange PESONet batch as alternative, (c) re-initiate payment after resolution, (d) if payment deadline is at risk (e.g., BIR tax deadline): escalate to CFO for emergency resolution
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: 30–60 min per rejection</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1342_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1342_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1342_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1342_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1342_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-294 (ensure controlled execution — Banking &amp; Payments (PA-18.2).) | - operational: dual authorization, vendor master validation, and pre-submission verification checklist; operational: morning cash position review and pre-funding arrangement; operational: early processing and maintaining alternative banking relationships for contingency
Owner: Treasury Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1342_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1342_Annotation14" targetRef="W1342_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
