    <bpmn:process id="W_W1343" name="W1343. Petty Cash Fund Lifecycle, Custodian Accountability &amp; Periodic Replenishment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Small, urgent business expense requiring cash payment; or petty cash fund replenishment request (fund depleted to ~20% of authorized level); or annual petty cash policy review
Frequency: ~50–80 petty cash disbursements per store per month; replenishment every 2–4 weeks per store; annual policy review
Volume: 200 stores × the authorized petty cash fund of PHP 20,000 per store = ~PHP 4.2M total petty cash float (incl. DC floats, per profile §10.4); ~10,000–16,000 disbursements/month chain-wide
Owner: Store Manager (custodian)
Participants: Cash Office Clerk, Store Manager, Regional Manager (approval &gt; PHP 5,000), AP Clerk (replenishment processing), Finance Controller, Banking &amp; Cash-Management Specialist
Source: workflow W1343 — Petty Cash Fund Lifecycle, Custodian Accountability &amp; Periodic Replenishment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1343_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1343_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1343_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1343_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1343_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1343_Lane2" name="Requester">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1343_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1343_Lane3" name="Internal Auditor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1343_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1343_Lane4" name="Finance Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1343_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1343_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1343_Start6" name="Small, urgent business expense requiring cash payment; or petty cash fund replenishment…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1343_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1343_Task7" name="Petty cash fund establishment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Petty cash fund establishment: For new stores per W16 or when existing fund amount is adjusted: (a) Store Manager requests petty cash fund authorization from Regional Manager: proposed amount, justification, (b) standard authorized levels: small stores (PHP 20,000), medium stores (PHP 30,000), large/flagship stores (PHP 50,000), (c) Finance Controller approves fund authorization and sets up petty cash GL account per store, (d) initial funding: Treasury transfers authorized amount to store bank account; Store Manager withdraws cash and secures in store safe per W541, (e) system records petty cash fund: store, authorized amount, custodian (Store Manager), establishment date
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Finance Controller
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1343_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1343_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1343_Task8" name="Petty cash disbursement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Petty cash disbursement: For each expense requiring petty cash: (a) requester (Department Supervisor, stock associate) submits Petty Cash Voucher: date, amount, purpose, payee, supporting documentation (receipt, quotation), (b) Store Manager reviews and approves: (i) is the expense legitimate business purpose?, (ii) is petty cash the appropriate payment method (vs. procurement card or standard PO)?, (iii) is the amount within petty cash policy limit (max PHP 5,000 per transaction; &gt; PHP 5,000 requires Regional Manager approval), (iv) is supporting documentation adequate (official receipt from BIR-registered supplier preferred)?, (c) Cash Office Clerk disburses cash from petty cash fund, (d) requester signs Petty Cash Voucher acknowledging receipt, (e) voucher filed in petty cash binder with supporting documentation, (f) system logs disbursement: date, amount, purpose, payee, voucher number, custodian approval
Responsible (R): Requester / Cash Office Clerk / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5–10 min per disbursement</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1343_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1343_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1343_Task9" name="Periodic replenishment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Periodic replenishment: When petty cash fund is depleted to ~20% of authorized level (or every 4 weeks, whichever is first): (a) Store Manager prepares Petty Cash Replenishment Report: (i) summary of all disbursements since last replenishment: voucher number, date, amount, purpose, GL expense category, (ii) total disbursements = replenishment amount requested, (iii) remaining cash on hand (should equal ~20% of authorized fund), (iv) attach all Petty Cash Vouchers with supporting documentation (receipts), (b) Store Manager signs Replenishment Report certifying accuracy, (c) Regional Manager reviews and approves replenishment (spot-check 10% of vouchers for compliance), (d) AP Clerk processes replenishment per W7: creates AP voucher for replenishment amount, charges individual line items to appropriate GL expense accounts, (e) Treasury transfers replenishment amount to store bank account, (f) Store Manager withdraws cash and restores petty cash fund to authorized level
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Regional Manager / AP Clerk
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 30–60 min per replenishment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1343_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1343_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1343_Task10" name="Surprise petty cash count">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Surprise petty cash count: Internal Audit or Regional Manager conducts surprise petty cash count during store visits per W1174: (a) count actual cash on hand in petty cash fund, (b) total Petty Cash Vouchers since last replenishment, (c) verify: cash on hand + vouchers = authorized fund amount (imprest system), (d) sample 5 vouchers: verify supporting documentation, approval, GL coding accuracy, (e) flag any discrepancies: (i) shortage (cash + vouchers &lt; authorized) — potential theft or unvouchered disbursement, (ii) excess — possible commingling of personal cash or unrecorded deposits, (iii) missing receipts — non-compliance with documentation policy, (f) document findings and include in store LP compliance score per W1174
Responsible (R): Internal Auditor / Regional Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 15–20 min per count</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1343_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1343_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1343_Task11" name="Annual policy review &amp; fund adjustment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Annual policy review &amp; fund adjustment: Finance Controller reviews petty cash program annually: (a) analyze average replenishment frequency and amount by store — are fund levels appropriate?, (b) identify stores with unusually high or low petty cash activity — investigate for policy abuse or under-utilization, (c) review disbursement categories: are expenses legitimate or should any be routed through standard procurement?, (d) adjust authorized fund levels for stores with changing needs (new services, increased maintenance), (e) update petty cash policy: transaction limits, documentation requirements, approval thresholds, (f) communicate policy changes to all Store Managers
Responsible (R): Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 day/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1343_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1343_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1343_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1343_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1343_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-294 (ensure controlled execution — Banking &amp; Payments (PA-18.2).) | - operational: requiring at minimum a handwritten receipt signed by payee; operational: automated replenishment trigger at 20% threshold and standard 3-day AP processing SLA; operational: surprise counts, Regional Manager spot-checks, and GL expense analysis for unusual patterns
Owner: Store Manager (custodian)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1343_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1343_Annotation13" targetRef="W1343_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1343_Flow15" sourceRef="W1343_Start6" targetRef="W1343_Task7" />
