    <bpmn:process id="W_W1294" name="W1294. Import Letter of Credit (LC) Application &amp; Bank Coordination" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Import purchase order confirmed with vendor requiring LC payment terms; or existing LC approaching expiry requiring amendment
Frequency: ~50–80 new LC applications per month; ~10–20 LC amendments per month
Volume: ~40% of COGS from imports; ~400–600 TEUs/month; LC value typically PHP 5M–50M per shipment
Owner: Treasury Analyst
Participants: Treasury Analyst, Import Coordinator, Category Manager, Bank Relationship Manager, AP Clerk
Source: workflow W1294 — Import Letter of Credit (LC) Application &amp; Bank Coordination</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1294_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1294_Lane1" name="Import Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1294_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1294_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1294_Lane2" name="Treasury Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1294_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1294_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1294_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1294_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1294_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1294_Lane3" name="Bank">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1294_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1294_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1294_Start5" name="Import purchase order confirmed with vendor requiring LC payment terms; or existing LC…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1294_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1294_Task6" name="LC requirement identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: LC requirement identification: Import Coordinator confirms LC requirement for import PO: (a) vendor payment terms specify LC (vs. TT/telegraphic transfer), (b) determine LC type (sight, usance), LC amount, validity period, and latest shipment date per PO terms, (c) identify required shipping documents: commercial invoice, packing list, bill of lading, certificate of origin, insurance certificate, inspection certificate (if applicable), (d) communicate LC requirements to Treasury Analyst with PO details and urgency
Responsible (R): Import Coordinator
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 15 min/LC</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1294_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1294_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1294_Task7" name="LC application preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: LC application preparation: Treasury Analyst prepares LC application for the bank: (a) complete bank LC application form with: applicant (BuildRight Depot, Inc.), beneficiary (vendor), LC amount (in USD or vendor currency), LC type, expiry date, shipping terms (FOB, CIF, CFR per Incoterms), required documents, (b) attach supporting documents: import PO, proforma invoice, import permit (if applicable), (c) calculate bank margin requirement: LC amount × margin rate (10–30%) and confirm available credit facility
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Corporate Treasurer
Duration: 30 min/LC</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1294_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1294_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1294_Task8" name="LC issuance by bank">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: LC issuance by bank: Treasury Analyst submits LC application to relationship bank (BDO, BPI, Metrobank, or Chinabank per credit facility allocation): (a) bank reviews application and issues LC via SWIFT MT700 to vendor&#x27;s bank (advising bank), (b) bank confirms LC issuance and debits margin from BuildRight&#x27;s account, (c) Treasury Analyst records LC in treasury management system: LC number, amount, expiry, vendor, margin held, (d) LC advice sent to Import Coordinator for vendor notification
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst / Bank
Accountable (A): Corporate Treasurer
Duration: 1–3 business days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1294_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1294_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1294_Task9" name="Shipping document review &amp; negotiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Shipping document review &amp; negotiation: Upon vendor shipment, vendor&#x27;s bank presents shipping documents to BuildRight&#x27;s issuing bank: (a) bank examines documents against LC terms (strict compliance required per UCP 600), (b) if documents comply: bank forwards documents to Treasury Analyst for payment authorization, (c) if discrepancies: bank flags discrepancies (common: late shipment, document date errors, quantity variance); Treasury Analyst coordinates with Import Coordinator to determine if discrepancy is acceptable or requires vendor amendment
Responsible (R): Bank / Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Corporate Treasurer
Duration: 3–5 business days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1294_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1294_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1294_Task10" name="Payment authorization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Payment authorization: For complying documents or accepted discrepancies: (a) Treasury Analyst reviews shipping documents: verify quantities match PO, shipping terms correct, insurance adequate, (b) authorize payment: for sight LC — payment within 5 business days of document compliance, for usance LC — payment at maturity date, (c) system records AP invoice with LC payment method and due date, (d) bank debits BuildRight&#x27;s USD account at payment date and releases margin
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Corporate Treasurer
Duration: 15 min/LC</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1294_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1294_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1294_Task11" name="LC closure &amp; margin release">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: LC closure &amp; margin release: Upon payment completion: (a) bank releases margin (10–30% of LC value) back to BuildRight&#x27;s account, (b) Treasury Analyst confirms margin release in treasury system, (c) update available credit facility balance, (d) archive LC documents for BIR and customs audit trail per W77, (e) feed LC cost (issuance fee, amendment fees, discrepancy fees) to AP for vendor chargeback negotiation per W7 if applicable
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst / Bank
Accountable (A): Corporate Treasurer
Duration: 15 min/LC</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1294_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1294_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1294_Task12" name="Monthly LC portfolio management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Monthly LC portfolio management: Treasury Analyst compiles monthly LC portfolio report: (a) total outstanding LC value by bank and currency, (b) total margin held by bank, (c) LC utilization rate vs. approved credit facility, (d) discrepancy rate (LCs with discrepancies ÷ total LCs) — target &lt;10%, (e) average LC processing time (application to issuance), (f) LC cost analysis (fees as % of import value)
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Corporate Treasurer
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1294_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1294_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1294_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1294_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1294_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-294 (ensure controlled execution — Banking &amp; Payments (PA-18.2).) | - operational: FX hedging per W80
Owner: Treasury Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1294_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1294_Annotation14" targetRef="W1294_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
