    <bpmn:process id="W_W5559" name="W5559. Vendor Payment-Diversion &amp; Business Email Compromise (BEC) Fraud Event Response &amp; Recovery Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Discovery that a completed BuildRight disbursement was diverted to a fraudster-controlled account — the vendor reports payments unpaid after a bank-detail change, a bank flags a beneficiary anomaly, or review finds a vendor-master bank change immediately followed by payment runs — or the near-miss variant: an executive-impersonation urgent-transfer request intercepted before execution
Frequency: Low-single-digit attempted events per year — BEC is named in this PA&#x27;s own risk register as the most common payment-fraud vector in Philippine corporate treasury; successful diversion is rarer wherever CTL-59&#x27;s callback discipline held
Volume: 1 event × the diverted tranche (typically 1–6 payments inside one W1362 run; a PHP 0.3M–8M exposure band) × the recovery surface (bank recall window, beneficiary bank, police case, crime-policy claim)
Owner: Treasury Manager
Participants: CFO, AP Manager (VS-15.1 invoice-match chain W556/W770), Vendor Master Data steward (VS-29 change audit trail), Legal Counsel (VS-100), Fraud Management Lead (VS-125), IT Security (W383; mailbox audit per W5518), Insurance Coordinator (VS-26 crime/fidelity policy), Internal Audit (VS-21), the affected vendor&#x27;s pre-change verified contacts, BuildRight&#x27;s bank fraud desk and the beneficiary bank, PNP Anti-Cybercrime Group
Source: workflow W5559 — Vendor Payment-Diversion &amp; Business Email Compromise (BEC) Fraud Event Response &amp; Recovery Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5559_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5559_Lane1" name="Treasury Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5559_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5559_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5559_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5559_Lane2" name="IT Security">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5559_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5559_Lane3" name="Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5559_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5559_Lane4" name="Treasury">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5559_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5559_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5559_Lane5" name="Insurance Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5559_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5559_Lane6" name="Internal Audit">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5559_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5559_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5559_Start8" name="Discovery that a completed BuildRight disbursement was diverted to a fraudster-controlled…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5559_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5559_Task9" name="Verify &amp; freeze">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Verify &amp; freeze: confirm the fraud with the vendor through the pre-change verified contact held in the W317 account records — never any contact detail supplied on the change request or in the fraudulent correspondence; freeze all pending payments to the vendor; suspend the vendor-master record from further runs
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager / AP Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Same day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5559_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5559_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5559_Task10" name="Bank recall &amp; trace race">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Bank recall &amp; trace race: fraud-desk engagement on both sides (remitting bank + beneficiary bank) within hours — PESONet/InstaPay recall odds collapse after the first day; document the recall trail; request a beneficiary-bank freeze while funds remain
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager / Bank Fraud Desk
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: First 24–72 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5559_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5559_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5559_Task11" name="Classify &amp; forensically contain">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Classify &amp; forensically contain: internal (collusion/insider — the VS-29 vendor-master change audit trail shows who changed what, when, from where) vs external (mailbox compromise — export mail rules and M365 audit logs per W5518; W383 handles the host/incident core); executive-impersonation variant → preserve the correspondence and call logs
Responsible (R): IT Security / Internal Audit
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5559_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5559_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5559_Task12" name="Police &amp; regulatory referral">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Police &amp; regulatory referral: sworn affidavit and evidence pack (change requests, before/after bank-detail snapshots, payment confirmations, recall trail) to PNP ACG under RA 10175; AML officer consulted where a covered-entity channel (VS-86 estate) touched the flow
Responsible (R): Legal / Treasury
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5559_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5559_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5559_Task13" name="Honest-ledger treatment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Honest-ledger treatment: reverse the misdirected application — the diverted payment does not discharge the payable; keep the vendor&#x27;s aging truthful; park the loss in a fraud-recovery suspense account; written notice to the vendor and re-payment of the still-owed invoices over verified rails
Responsible (R): Treasury / AP / Corporate Accounting
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5559_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5559_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5559_Task14" name="Recovery &amp; insurance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Recovery &amp; insurance: fidelity/crime-policy notice filed within the policy window (VS-26); restitution pursued through the criminal case; no double-claim against the bank absent its own control failure
Responsible (R): Insurance Coordinator / Legal
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1–4 months</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5559_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5559_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5559_Task15" name="Verification retrofit &amp; sweep">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Verification retrofit &amp; sweep: dual-channel callback audit of every vendor bank-detail change in the trailing 90 days; cooling-off window before the first payment to any changed account (the CTL-59 extension); callback evidence attached to the master-data change record; red-card briefing to Treasury and AP on the urgent-transfer impersonation script
Responsible (R): Treasury / Vendor Master Data / Internal Audit
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5559_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5559_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5559_Task16" name="Case closure &amp; intelligence">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Case closure &amp; intelligence: full case file to the VS-21/VS-125 fraud-intelligence registers; loss and recovery reconciled; the control-failure note documented for the CTL-59 control owner
Responsible (R): Internal Audit / Fraud Management
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5559_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5559_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5559_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5559_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5559_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-59 (prevent unauthorized bank account changes) | - CTL-62 (ensure electronic banking security) | - operational: dual-channel callback on every bank-detail change before the next payment run; diverted funds never netted against the vendor payable; bank recall initiated within 24 hours of discovery
Owner: Treasury Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5559_Assoc19" sourceRef="W5559_Annotation18" targetRef="W5559_Start8" associationDirection="None" />
